---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/base-layout.astro";

export function getStaticPaths() {
    return [{ params: { locale: "en" } }, { params: { locale: "zh" } }];
}

const { locale = "en" } = Astro.params;
---

<BaseLayout
    title="About"
    locale={locale}
    headerTarget="custom"
    footerType="index"
>
    <!-- 右上角的連結先被移除，等未來想到要連去哪再補上，去site.json加 -->

    <div class="project-page grid-12">
        <!-- 獨立左側選單列 -->
        <aside class="about-menu mobile-off">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <a href="mailto:hello@ercoffice.net">Email</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <a href={`/${locale}/Exhibitions/`}>Exhibitions</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <a
                        href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1eLl6lkIzNF7iF7ZSYUgnxeBCQjENkT9v?usp=sharing"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    >
                        Press kits
                        <img src="/imgs/arrow.svg" class="arrow" alt="" />
                    </a>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </aside>

        <!-- MAIN CONTENT -->
        <div class="project-content">
            <!-- 01 ERCO LAI -->

            <section class="project-section grid-12" id="erco-lai">
                <div class="col-12">
                    <p class="title-XL lang-en">
                        My design approach is listening to materials through
                        hands-on experiments and shaping them in the most
                        "natural" way. Through my practice, I attempt to find
                        beauty in the balance between design control and
                        material spontaneity.
                    </p>

                    <p class="title-XL lang-zh">
                        我透過製作理解材質，也透過物質重新思考造形。讓設計的意圖與材料的自發性彼此協商，在不斷實驗之中尋找事物形成的另一種可能。
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="project-section grid-12" id="">
                <div class="about-text-block col-7">
                    <h6>About</h6>
                    <p class="project-title">Erco Lai</p>

                    <p class="about-text lang-en">
                        Erco Lai is an interdisciplinary artist / designer
                        working across sculptural objects, spatial
                        installations, and experimental fabrication. His
                        practice explores the relationships between matter,
                        form, and craft, drawing from geological formations,
                        natural forces, and industrial processes. Combining
                        hands-on experimentation with computational tools, he
                        approaches making as a dialogue between physical
                        intuition and technological precision. Rather than
                        imposing predetermined shapes upon materials, he
                        embraces their resistance, deformation, and
                        unpredictability as part of the creative process. For
                        Lai, making is both a means of artistic expression and a
                        way of understanding the material world. Working within
                        the conditions of the post-industrial era, he
                        reinterprets materials and manufacturing techniques as
                        artistic media. His practice moves from intimate objects
                        to large-scale installations, exploring how gravity,
                        movement, and environmental forces can shape new forms
                        and spatial experiences.
                    </p>

                    <p class="about-text lang-zh">
                        賴亭安 / Erco Lai
                        是一位跨領域藝術家與設計師，創作涵蓋雕塑、空間裝置、材料研究與實驗性製造。他以材料、造形與工藝之間的關係為核心，從地質生成、自然力量與工業製程中尋找線索，探索物質如何在不同的技術與環境條件下形成獨特的表現語言。出身於工業設計背景的他，將製作視為一種透過材料進行思考的方式，在身體的直覺與技術的精準之間往返，探索人為意圖與物質特性如何共同參與形式的生成。
                        <br />
                        <br />
                        透過持續的動手實驗、運算設計與數位製造，他觀察材料如何回應壓力、限制與變化。相較於將預先設定的形式施加於材料，他更傾向從物質本身的特性出發，讓阻力、變形與不可預測的反應成為造形的條件。對他而言，工藝不僅是既有技法的延續，也是一種透過雙手、工具與物質累積的感知與知識。機器與程式並非單純執行設計的工具，而是拓展身體經驗與造形想像的媒介。他試圖在傳統工藝與當代製造技術之間建立新的關係，將製程中的偶然與材料的抗性轉化為藝術表現的可能。
                        <br />
                        <br />
                        <span class="mobile-off">
                            隨著研究與實踐的發展，他的創作逐漸從日常物件延伸至雕塑與大型空間裝置。當形式進入更大的尺度，重力、運動、結構與周遭環境便成為不可分割的創作條件。他試圖讓作品不只是被放置於空間中的物件，而能回應場域，呈現物質與外力相互作用的過程。在後工業時代的生產條件中，他持續重新詮釋材料與製造技術的藝術潛力，在自然與人為、機械與直覺、控制與偶然之間尋找不同的形式。對他而言，造物不只是實現構想，更是一種理解世界、參與物質轉化的方式。
                        </span>
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="about-image col-5">
                    <img
                        src="/imgs/portrait.jpg"
                        alt="Erco Lai portrait"
                        loading="lazy"
                    />
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="project-section grid-12 mobile-off" id="">
                <!-- AWARDS -->
                <div class="about-text-block col-6">
                    <p class="about-title">Award & Grant</p>

                    <div class="project-text">
                        <p>2023 Stimuleringsfonds Opencall Milan Design Week</p>
                        <p>2023 The Index Project — Nominees</p>
                        <p>2022 STARTS Prize, Ars Electronica — Nomination</p>
                        <p>2022 Guiltlessplastic — Finalist</p>
                        <p>2022 Creative Industries Fund NL — Starting Grant</p>
                        <p>
                            2021 MA Industrial Design Department Award —
                            Nomination
                        </p>
                        <p>2018 Golden Pin Design Award, Taiwan</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- EXHIBITIONS -->
                <div class="about-text-block col-6">
                    <p class="about-title">Exhibitions</p>

                    <div class="project-text">
                        <p>2024 Milan Design Week — ISOLA</p>
                        <p>2024 Stockholm Furniture Fair — Greenhouse</p>
                        <p>2023 London Design Week — Mint Gallery</p>
                        <p>
                            2023 International Steel Sculpture Festival,
                            Kaohsiung
                        </p>
                        <p>2023 Maison&Objet, Paris</p>
                        <p>2023 ALCOVA, Milan</p>
                        <p>2022 Object Rotterdam</p>
                        <p>2021 Dutch Design Week</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- COLLABORATIONS -->
                <div class="about-text-block col-12">
                    <p class="about-title">Selected Clients & Collaborations</p>

                    <p class="project-text">
                        Blue City (NL), Biophilica (UK), TPCreative (TW), Binary
                        Pottery (TW), Hevo deco (TW), 20MM (TW)
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 02 ERCOFFICE -->

            <section class="project-section grid-12" id="ercoffice">
                <div class="about-image col-12">
                    <img
                        title="Photo: Ronald Smits"
                        src="/imgs/ercoffice.jpg"
                        alt="ercoffice studio"
                        loading="lazy"
                    />
                </div>
            </section>
            <section class="project-section grid-12" id="">
                <div class="col-12">
                    <p class="title-XL lang-en">
                        A design office aims to cooperate with material-focused
                        developers, scientists or start-ups to elevate future
                        materials from experiments into the context of daily
                        life by giving matter meaningful forms.
                    </p>

                    <p class="title-XL lang-zh">
                        我們不只是試著製造不同的事物，也試著重新理解事物可以如何被製造。
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="project-section grid-12" id="">
                <div class="about-text-block col-7">
                    <h6>About</h6>
                    <p class="project-title">ercoffice</p>

                    <p class="about-text lang-en">
                        Founded by Erco Lai, ercoffice is a research-led design
                        practice working across material research, craft, object
                        development, and spatial design. Guided by Make Things
                        Like Earth, the studio explores alternative methods of
                        making through material experimentation, computational
                        processes, and interdisciplinary collaboration.
                        Positioned between science, craft, industry, nature, and
                        culture, ercoffice approaches design as a means of
                        connecting different forms of knowledge. Rather than
                        treating nature merely as a source of inspiration or
                        industry solely as a means of production, the studio
                        investigates both as systems of material transformation,
                        seeking new approaches to form giving. Central to this
                        practice is the idea of an experimental factory: an
                        evolving environment where materials, techniques,
                        technologies, and people come together to develop
                        methods of making. From traditional craftsmanship to
                        digital fabrication, the studio explores how existing
                        knowledge and production processes can be adapted,
                        combined, and reinterpreted. Working with material
                        developers, scientists, engineers, manufacturers, and
                        cultural institutions, ercoffice connects experimental
                        research with practical and cultural applications.
                        Through independent inquiries and commissioned projects,
                        the studio translates technical knowledge and material
                        discoveries into objects, products, and spatial
                        interventions. By bringing together research, craft, and
                        collaboration, ercoffice continues to explore methods of
                        form giving and new possibilities for making in the
                        post-industrial era.
                    </p>

                    <p class="about-text lang-zh">
                        ercoffice
                        鈋谷賦形事物所是一個研究導向的跨領域設計實踐，工作涵蓋材料研究、工藝實驗、物件開發與空間設計。以
                        Make Things Like Earth
                        為思想方向，透過材料、技術與跨領域合作，探索後工業時代的賦形造物之法。
                        事物所處於科學、工藝、工業、自然與文化的交會之間，將設計視為連結不同知識與技術的方式。我們不將自然僅視為造形靈感，也不將工業單純視為生產工具，而是從兩者的物質轉化過程中，尋找新的製作方法。
                        我們將 Factory / 工廠
                        重新想像為一個開放的實驗場域，讓材料、工藝、技術與不同領域的知識在此交流。從傳統手工到數位製造，透過實驗、轉用與組合既有技術，發展不同的造形與製造方法。
                        透過與材料開發者、科學研究者、工程師、製造業者及文化機構的合作，事物所連結實驗研究與實際應用。從自主探索到委託專案，將技術知識與材料研究轉化為物件、產品及空間構成，持續拓展設計與製造的可能性。
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="about-image col-5">
                    <img
                        src="/imgs/ercoffice-position.svg"
                        alt="ercoffice diagram"
                        loading="lazy"
                    />
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
